<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Surveys' cross-section surface, carved into its own leaf project because its only
    consumer outside the section is still in Base: SendSurveyReminderJob
    (Humans.Infrastructure/Jobs), which stays there because recurring jobs are named by
    concrete type in Shell's UseHumansRecurringJobs roll-call and there is no discovery
    seam for them yet (design §15.6b). A Contracts/ *folder* inside Humans.Surveys would
    therefore make Base reference a section and cycle (design §15.5b,
    memory/architecture/section-project-cycle-fix.md).

    It holds exactly one interface. Nothing else Surveys exposes has a consumer outside
    the section — the three controllers, the DI registration and the section's own tests
    are the whole fan-in — so the rest stays internal. There is deliberately no
    ISurveyServiceRead here: the read interface shipped empty in v1 and no section ever
    consumed it (design §15 step 5, "keep an interface only where something needs the seam").

    References Humans.Interfaces only.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Interfaces\Humans.Interfaces.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
